    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0389" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.55/29.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Gonzales.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Chinese Legation informs Department that suspension for sixty days of prohibition
                    against Chinese immigration into Cuba will expire end of May.</p>
                <pb facs="0390" n="274" xml:id="pg274"/>
                <p>You are instructed to cooperate with Chinese Chargé d’Affaires in an effort to
                    induce Cuban Government to allow the suspending order to remain in force pending
                    conclusion of treaty between China and Cuba.</p>
                <p>Report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
